From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ram: generate_ram -periphery verilog, the core routed
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

generate_ram takes -periphery verilog and -wrapper_verilog: the routed
block is the core, <name>_core, and the periphery is written as a
Verilog module, <name>, around it, for a parent's synthesis to map and
place with its own logic. The netlist puts each of the core's pins
where its connections land, for a macro placer to orient the core by;
generate_ram drops those and places the pins on the core's edges as it
does for any block, so the core routes. -periphery unplaced, which
leaves the periphery unplaced inside the block, stays
generate_ram_netlist's, for a flow that places it; generate_ram stops
on it with RAM-0098.

Tested: src/ram/test/periphery_verilog_asap7.tcl, which routes the core
in the commit that follows.

Commit 21 of 23 in OpenROAD #11723, carried here from it. Not
upstreamed; retires at a //:bump onto an OpenROAD that has it.
---
 src/ram/README.md   |  2 +-
 src/ram/src/ram.tcl | 29 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 2 files changed, 28 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/ram/README.md b/src/ram/README.md
index 3a36bd2cab..75ac7f6379 100644
--- a/src/ram/README.md
+++ b/src/ram/README.md
@@ -94,7 +94,7 @@ generate_ram [-mask_size bits]
 | `-write_priority` | Where two write ports write the same word in one cycle: `last`, the last port's data; or `or`, the OR of every writing port's data, as RTL that merges its writes with an OR describes it (firtool's register files). `or` drops a word's priority logic, an inverter and an AND2 per port but the last. Default: `last`. |
 | `-service_columns {every sites}` | An empty column `sites` sites wide after every `every` storage columns: room inside the array for the buffers a parent flow inserts on the long nets that cross it, where the array is otherwise full. Default: none. |
 | `-bank_column_layout interleaved\|contiguous` | With banks, how a row's words share its columns: `interleaved`, bit by bit as the column mux lays them out; or `contiguous`, each word's bits side by side with its select column after them. Contiguous keeps a word's selects and write enables as short as its own bits, where interleaved runs them the whole row; the read trees then cross the row instead. Default: `interleaved`. |
-| `-periphery`, `-pin_layer`, `-wrapper_verilog` | `generate_ram_netlist` only. `unplaced` leaves the periphery (address inverters and registers, decoders, select buffers, each word's select cell, the input buffers) for a parent to place, size and buffer; the outline is the placed core and a row, and each pin sits where its connections land, on `-pin_layer`'s tracks, for a macro placer before the parent dissolves the core into its rows. `verilog` makes the core a block of its own, `<name>_core`, and writes the periphery to `-wrapper_verilog` as a Verilog module, `<name>`, around it: assigns of the cells' functions, for synthesis to map with the parent. Default: `placed`. |
+| `-periphery`, `-pin_layer`, `-wrapper_verilog` | `unplaced` and `-pin_layer` are `generate_ram_netlist`'s only, for a flow that places the periphery itself; `generate_ram` takes `placed` and `verilog`, routes the core and puts its pins on its edges. `unplaced` leaves the periphery (address inverters and registers, decoders, select buffers, each word's select cell, the input buffers) for a parent to place, size and buffer; the outline is the placed core and a row, and each pin sits where its connections land, on `-pin_layer`'s tracks, for a macro placer before the parent dissolves the core into its rows. `verilog` makes the core a block of its own, `<name>_core`, and writes the periphery to `-wrapper_verilog` as a Verilog module, `<name>`, around it: assigns of the cells' functions, for synthesis to map with the parent. Default: `placed`. |
 | `-cells` | The cell for a role (`inv`, `and2`, `buffer`, `clock_gate`, `aoi22`, `ao22`, `or2`, `nand2`, `nor2`, `tie`, `addr_flop`), instead of the smallest the libraries have of its function. An AOI22 or AO22 given is checked by its truth table. Default: the smallest of each. |
 | `-name` | The block's and the behavioral model's name. Default: `RAM<words>x<bits>`. |
 | `-decoder` | `row`: a decoder per row, an AND2 chain over the row address, the column mux selecting within the row. `word`: a balanced AND2 tree over each word's whole address, as with banks; shallower for the read path. Default: `row`. |
diff --git a/src/ram/src/ram.tcl b/src/ram/src/ram.tcl
index bd1f4e1948..6532bbe572 100644
--- a/src/ram/src/ram.tcl
+++ b/src/ram/src/ram.tcl
@@ -337,6 +337,8 @@ sta::define_cmd_args "generate_ram" {[-mask_size bits]
                                      [-max_tap_dist value]
                                      [-use_latch value]
                                      [-write_behavioral_verilog filename]
+                                     [-periphery placed|verilog]
+                                     [-wrapper_verilog file]
                                      [-tracks file]
                                      }
 
@@ -352,10 +354,15 @@ proc generate_ram { args } {
            -banks -bank_columns -bank_order -rb_ports -register_read_address
            -write_style -write_priority
            -cells -name -decoder -bit_folds -service_columns
-           -bank_column_layout -tracks } flags {}
+           -bank_column_layout -periphery -wrapper_verilog -tracks } flags {}
 
   sta::check_argc_eq0 "generate_ram" $args
 
+  if { [info exists keys(-periphery)] && $keys(-periphery) == "unplaced" } {
+    utl::error RAM 98 "generate_ram routes the block; -periphery unplaced\
+      is generate_ram_netlist's, for a flow that places the periphery."
+  }
+
   if { [info exists keys(-tracks)] && ![file readable $keys(-tracks)] } {
     utl::error RAM 97 "-tracks file $keys(-tracks) is not readable."
   }
@@ -408,11 +415,19 @@ proc generate_ram { args } {
   foreach key {-banks -bank_columns -bank_order -rb_ports -register_read_address
                -write_style -write_priority
                -cells -name -decoder -bit_folds -service_columns
-               -bank_column_layout} {
+               -bank_column_layout -periphery -wrapper_verilog} {
     if { [info exists keys($key)] } {
       lappend ram_netlist_args $key $keys($key)
     }
   }
+  # the netlist places a Verilog periphery's core pins on a layer of its
+  # own; generate_ram places them again on its edges
+  if {
+    [info exists keys(-periphery)] && $keys(-periphery) == "verilog"
+    && [info exists keys(-hor_layer)]
+  } {
+    lappend ram_netlist_args -pin_layer [lindex $keys(-hor_layer) 0]
+  }
 
   if { [info exists keys(-inv_cell)] } {
     lappend ram_netlist_args -inv_cell $keys(-inv_cell)
@@ -520,6 +535,16 @@ proc generate_ram { args } {
     make_tracks -x_offset 0 -y_offset 0
   }
 
+  # -periphery verilog: the netlist put each of the core's pins where
+  # its connections land, for a macro placer to orient the core by;
+  # a routed core takes its pins on its edges instead
+  if { [info exists keys(-periphery)] && $keys(-periphery) == "verilog" } {
+    foreach bterm [[ord::get_db_block] getBTerms] {
+      foreach bpin [$bterm getBPins] {
+        odb::dbBPin_destroy $bpin
+      }
+    }
+  }
   ram::ram_pinplacer $ver_name $hor_name
 
   ram::ram_filler $filler_cells
